  #line-at(70.824pt, 238.49pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 259.13pt, "Mobile ion migration strongly influences the electrical response and current–voltage hysteresis ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 279.89pt, "of perovskite solar cells. However, quantitative determination of ionic transport parameters ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 300.53pt, "typically requires transient measurements, extensive numerical simulations, and/or fitting ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 321.29pt, "procedures involving multiple uncertain parameters. Here, we present an analytical model that ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 341.93pt, "establishes a direct relationship between capacitance–frequency (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.1pt, 341.93pt, "C–f)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(405.46pt, 341.93pt, " characteristics and ionic ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 362.69pt, "transport properties in perovskite solar cells, while accounting for interlayer effects. The model ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 383.35pt, "describes the transition from the ion-screened depletion capacitance at low frequencies to the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 404.11pt, "geometric capacitance at high frequencies and demonstrates that the characteristic transition ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 424.75pt, "frequency provides a direct measure of the dielectric relaxation time for ions. Furthermore, the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 445.39pt, "model establishes a quantitative connection between ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(351.67pt, 445.39pt, "C–f")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(369.07pt, 445.39pt, " characteristics and scan-rate-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 466.15pt, "dependent current–voltage hysteresis, enabling prediction of the scan-rate window in which ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 486.79pt, "maximum hysteresis occurs. Drift–diffusion simulations show excellent agreement with the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 507.55pt, "analytical predictions over wide ranges of ion density, ion mobility, transport-layer mobility ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 528.19pt, "and doping concentration. Experimental measurements confirm the predicted correlation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 548.98pt, "between capacitance and hysteresis. By providing a direct, physically transparent, and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 569.62pt, "computationally efficient route for extracting ionic transport parameters from routine ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 590.38pt, "impedance measurements, this work offers a practical tool for quantifying ion migration and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 611.02pt, "understanding dynamic phenomena in perovskite solar cells. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 652.42pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 673.18pt, "Metal-halide perovskites have emerged as one of the most important semiconductor materials ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 693.84pt, "for next-generation photovoltaics owing to their exceptional optoelectronic properties, low-cost ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 714.6pt, "processing, and rapidly increasing power-conversion efficiencies. Since the first demonstration ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 735.24pt, "of perovskite-based solar cells, device efficiencies have increased from below 4% to 28%, [1] ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 756pt, "placing perovskite solar cells (PSCs) among the most promising photovoltaic technologies for ")
]

